# detail
Number of changes: 1

1. Modified | Implementation code block
   Replaced explicit checks and clipping logic in the method body with a call to `_clip_with_one_bound`.
   The original implementation included:

   * Conditional statement: test whether `threshold` contained NA values and raise `ValueError`;
   * Conditional statement: test whether `threshold` was a numeric scalar and return `self._clip_with_scalar(threshold, None)`;
   * Assignment statement: assign `self.ge(threshold, axis=axis) | isnull(self)` to `subset`;
   * Return statement: return `self.where(subset, threshold, axis=axis)`.

   The new implementation includes:

   * Return statement: return `self._clip_with_one_bound(threshold, method=self.ge, axis=axis, inplace=inplace)`.
